00:10:33,067 --> 00:10:33,780
Got it.

147
00:10:33,780 --> 00:10:36,531
What do I need to remember?

148
00:10:37,067 --> 00:10:41,191
git rebase --abort restores everything as before the rebase.

149
00:10:41,733 --> 00:10:47,178
Only one rebase at a time; git status tells you if one is in progress.

150
00:10:47,733 --> 00:10:53,748
After a completed rebase, ORIG_HEAD / reflog bring the old branch back.

151
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:59,043
I keep hearing about continuing a rebase.

152
00:10:59,043 --> 00:11:00,684
What is it, really?

153
00:11:01,233 --> 00:11:04,661
git rebase --continue resumes a paused rebase.

154
00:11:04,661 --> 00:11:07,046
A rebase pauses for two reasons:

155
00:11:07,046 --> 00:11:10,995
a conflict (lesson 64) or an edit stop you asked for.

156
00:11:10,995 --> 00:11:19,043
We use edit to change an old commit in the middle of the history, and the next commits follow automatically.

157
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:25,200
